# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); an `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapted from [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n's own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy met automatische provisioning:** V1 poorten alle toegang via de gedeelde Keycloak OIDC-client (oauth2-proxy rand). Openresty stuurt de gewaarmerkte identiteit door naar n8n als vertrouwd `Remote-Email` kop (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, aangepast uit [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-so](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) leest die kop, auto-voorzieningen een lokale n8n gebruiker bij eerste aanmelding, en problemen n8n's eigen sessie cookie Keycloak gebruiker landt rechtstreeks in de workflow editor, zonder seconde, n8n-lokale aanmeldstap."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); an ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapted from `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n’s own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy met automatische provisioning:** V1 poorten alle toegang via de gedeelde Keycloak OIDC-client (oauth2-proxy rand). Openresty stuurt de gewaarmerkte identiteit door naar n8n als vertrouwd ``Remote-Email`` kop (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, aangepast uit `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) leest die kop, auto-voorzieningen een lokale n8n gebruiker bij eerste aanmelding, en problemen n8n Keycloak gebruiker landt rechtstreeks in de workflow editor, zonder seconde, n8n-lokale aanmeldstap."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's eigen SAML login tegen Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml))Geen proxy. Ongeauthenticeerde verzoeken raakte de Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, die doorverwijst naar Keycloak; de bewering komt terug op `/saml/acs` en een echte SuiteCRM sessie, dus de app maakt zijn eigen geauthentiseerde UI inclusief de logout control. Accounts worden gemaakt bij eerste aanmelding van de bewering (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), en het IdP ondertekeningscertificaat wordt gelezen van Keycloak's wereld descriptor door [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) bij het opstarten, over de Tor SOCKS proxy wanneer de uitgevende instelling een ui is, omdat een `.onion` uitgevende instelling is rechtstreeks niet op te lossen. `/auth` blijft bereikbaar als de lokale break-glas login."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** is SuiteCRMEigen SAML-login tegen Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` blijft bereikbaar als de lokale break-glas login."

